!Modula2 -- Modula-2 on the BOX

Modula-2 (PIM 4 and ISO 10514-1) compiled to machine code in memory by
LLVM and run at once, inside the box.  The compiler is MacModula2's.

The shell
  Double-click !Modula2 (or *Modula2 -edit [<file>]) for the Modula-2
  shell: a window with a menu bar (File, Edit, Run, Help), the program,
  and its output below.  F5 saves, compiles and runs the program there;
  Shift-F5 runs it in a TaskWindow; Ctrl-F re-indents it; F10 the menu
  bar; F1 the manual.  File > Open lists the programs in a directory.

Files
  &A7B Modula2   a program module or an implementation module (.mod)
  &A7C M2Def     a definition module (.def)
  Double-click a program to run it: its output appears in a TaskWindow;
  a program that makes a Declaritive window runs as a task of its own.
  The modules a program imports are found beside it (Name/def and
  Name/mod, or def.Name and mod.Name), then in the standard library.

The command
  *Modula2 [-c] [-t] [-O0..3] <file> [<arguments>]
  *Modula2 -edit [<file>]   the shell
    -c       compile only and report errors as  file:line: error: text
    -t       give the compile time
    -O0..-O3 LLVM's optimisation (default -O2)
  Escape stops a program (as HALT).  A fault ends the run, not the box.

The library
  The ISO library (STextIO, SWholeIO, SRealIO, TextIO, SeqFile,
  StreamFile, RndFile, Strings, EXCEPTIONS, COROUTINES, ...), PIM's
  (InOut, ...), and two of the box's own:
  SWI          RISC OS SWIs by name or number, registers in and out:
               Call raises an exception on an error, XCall returns the
               error block.  Str copies a string for a SWI, GetStr reads
               one back, Addr checks that an address is RISC OS's.
               NEW'd memory and global variables are in a dynamic area
               ("Modula-2") and can be given to SWIs.
  Declaritive  desktop windows described in JSON (the Declaritive
               module): Init, Add, Create, Set, Get, Poll, CloseDown.
  Their definition modules are in the ROM, /usr/lib/modula2/boxdef.

Not on the box
  Cocoa, Objective-C, COM and Win32, inline x86 assembler, and building
  executables (programs are always compiled and run).

Examples
  Graphics go to the screen: run Figures and Bounce from the command line
  (F12): *Modula2 <Modula2$Dir>.Examples.Figures.  Double-click the rest.

  Hello       printing, and a SWI
  SWIs        by name and number, registers in and out, the X form's error
  Machine     time and date, OS version, memory, variables, the screen mode
  Files       a text file written and read back by SeqFile and TextIO
  Catalogue   OS_File: save, information, load; a directory by OS_GBPB
  Guess       a number guessing game: ReadInt, and a key by OS_Byte 129
  Figures     a CLASS hierarchy that draws itself with OS_Plot
  Bounce      an animation, with text placed by VDU 31 and coloured by VDU 17
  Life        Conway's Game of Life in text, drawn in place
  Classes     a class and a subclass, a method overridden
  Modules     a module of its own (def.Queues, mod.Queues): an opaque type,
              and its exception caught
  Sets        enumerations and sets: union, intersection, IN, INCL, EXCL
  Exceptions  RAISE, EXCEPT and FINALLY
  Coroutines  NEWPROCESS and TRANSFER
  Generators  coroutines as generators: primes and Fibonacci side by side
  Bench       a benchmark, timed
  Greeter     a desktop window from JSON, by the Declaritive module
  Calc        a calculator form: fields, buttons, an answer (Declaritive)
  ToDo        a to-do list: a list box, buttons and a clock (Declaritive)
